      "resolution": "Three-part construction. (a) The detector is proven against a POSITIVE fixture first: a synthetic settings.json that DOES wire the hook must be detected, or the arm fails. (b) Candidate settings files are resolved from every place one can really live: $REPO_ROOT/.claude/, the PRIMARY CHECKOUT's .claude/ (reached via `git rev-parse --git-common-dir` + dirname, since a linked worktree has none of its own), and $CLAUDE_PROJECT_DIR/.claude/ — settings.json and settings.local.json in each, deduplicated. (c) The proven detector is applied to each file that exists. In this worktree it really did reach and check /home/coreyt/projects/fathomdb/.claude/settings.json and settings.local.json, and both are clean. If NO settings file exists anywhere (fresh clone / CI) the arm passes with an explicit loud message saying the invariant holds vacuously and pointing at the proven detector, so the pass is never mistaken for a positive observation."
